  "notes": "Modified cash basis. Governmental fund statement (p5) rolls fund balance forward (1,103,957 -> 1,363,058, equal to governmental net position cash basis), so those are in beginning_cash/ending_cash. Business-type roll-forward uses net position (p3): 305,632 + receipts 2,063,474 - disbursements 1,854,111 - transfers 208,698 = 306,297. Business-type receipts from Statement of Activities (p2/p3): program charges, sewer capital grant 146,427, investment income 665, miscellaneous 12,949; no single printed total, receipts total computed. Governmental transfers 208,240 net (From (To) Other Funds). Balance sheet uses government-wide Total column; due from/to other funds are not eliminated in the total column. Budget schedule p10 is an all-funds schedule that includes a nursing home (not in basic statements) so fund_type per line is approximate (revenue lines all marked governmental with review; actual revenue 8,906,598 includes utilities and nursing home). Page 11 is the budget note. Read pages 1-11 of 11. Recheck: all-funds budget schedule (p10) lines that mix fund types were split with split_from using the governmental (p5) and proprietary (p2/p3/p8) figures; the Charges for Services residual 5,694,207 is assumed to be the Nursing Home (business-type). v8 re-trim added report p11 (trimmed p7, Proprietary Funds Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position, accrual basis): it adds nothing new for this cash-basis extraction (business-type figures stay on the modified cash basis from p2/p3 and the cash flow statement p8; its object-level accrual expenses would double count the p10 budget function lines). Its totals agree: operating revenues 1,917,259, transfers (208,698), accrual net position 3,087,148 -> 3,345,413 (reconciled to cash-basis 306,297 on report p10, not trimmed). Report pp10 and 12 are reconciliations only. Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p5, p8) replace the combined schedule.",
